The regular-action computation makes the "one action is never enough" half a theorem;
what remains is a finite assembly argument over the subgroup lattice, all of whose ingredients
(fixed-point counts, orbit counts) are already formalised in this thread.

the global structure correction has ensemble mean **exactly `1`** (both over
  the residue data and, via the Chinese remainder theorem, averaged over
  `N mod ∏p`), so no `O(1)` smoothness edge can exist at any `u`;

**first homology vanishes at every scale** for any point cloud on a line, so the conjectured
  degree-one prime barcode does not exist, and this is sharp: a planar four-point cloud does carry
  an essential class;

